customer: retired_accountant
problem: no_sound
brief:
	Fixing the sound closes the errand. He also misses Clippy (NoClippy, a corruption that has no problem file, because CompuFunDB doesn't handle corruption): when he opens an office program, WordPad shows Clippy's frame empty. Clippy is only noticed; there is no solution, and the player can call him once the computer is tested and report no success. From now on Clippy is gone from every computer; before, he was there.

== drop-off
set sign_no_clippy
(neutral) It's me. Again.
(problem) I'm so sorry.
- The sound is gone?
- Don't be sorry. I'm here for you!
(problem) The sound is gone again. And now the little paperclip in my letters is gone too.
(neutral) He always helped me with the tax letters.
- Did you touch the volume?
	(neutral) No!
	(problem) Well. I might have clicked the little speaker.
	- And what about the paperclip?
- The paperclip?
(problem) Yes, he sat in the corner and helped. Now there's only an empty note.
- You mean Clippy? That's weird... I'll take a look.
	(neutral) Thank you. I kind of miss him...
	- ... I'll call you with my findings.

== pick-up
(happy) Wow you are fast!
- Well... Clicking a checkbox once...
- I sure am!
(happy) It plays its little tune again!
(problem) And the paperclip?
- Honestly - that's super weird. I couldn't bring him back. It shouldn't affect anything though.
	(neutral) Oh. Well. He had a good run, the little fellow.
	- Yeah, I've never seen that happen before...
